<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>To seek that forlorn, wayward sheep,</l><l>You left the ninety-nine;</l><l>The sinner on Your shoulders bore;</l><l>Earth’s joy and heaven’s combine!</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>To You who give eternal life,</l><l>Good Shepherd, we give thanks;</l><l>You know our names—as we Your voice—</l><l>And hold us in Your hands.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>From many “folds” You led us out,</l><l>To be one flock divine;</l><l>Our Shepherd, Door, our Pasture too,</l><l>Through You real rest we find.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Dear Lamb, our Shepherd on the throne,</l><l>You guide us all the way</l><l>To springs of waters, founts of life;</l><l>Each tear You wipe away.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>Jesus, Great Shepherd of the Church,</l><l>How faithful is Your care—</l><l>Inclusive, gentle, rich, and strong,</l><l>Both present and fore’er.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>Grant us a shepherd’s heart, like Yours,</l><l>With tenderest concern;</l><l>To feed Your sheep, to nurse Your lambs,</l><l>Of You we all will learn.</l></lg>
<lg label="8."><l>May we be carers of men’s souls,</l><l>With You, Chief Shepherd dear;</l><l>A crown of glory we’ll receive,</l><l>The hour when You appear.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
